WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.050
Pass an electric current through salt
water, using two inert electrodes.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.810
At the negative electrode,
bubbles of hydrogen appear.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.530
But salt water is full of sodium ions.

4
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.350
So why don't you get sodium?

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.930
Electrolyse salt water.

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.910
Why do you get hydrogen at the
negative electrode, not sodium?

7
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.630
In this mission, you'll predict the
products of electrolysing aqueous solutions,

8
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.500
electrode by electrode.

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.150
You'll electrolyse water itself,

10
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.170
and see how concentration changes
what forms at the positive electrode.

11
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.930
Your mission: explain why
salt water gives hydrogen,

12
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.470
not sodium, at the negative electrode.
